    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0603" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/18516½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">18 June, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have gone very
                    carefully through this note and think it adequate and excellent. I have here and
                    there altered the wording, but nowhere the meaning of it.</p>
                <p>I showed it to Baker last evening, and he makes, after taking it away for careful
                    perusal, the enclosed suggestion, which I think an excellent one. They might as
                    well know at once <hi rendition="#underline">all</hi> that they will be up
                    against if they continue their present attitude.</p>
                <p>How will you send this,—by post or wire?</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d403-a1.xml" xpointer="d403-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
